{
  "mn146:0.1": "Middle Discourses 146 ",
  "mn146:0.2": "Advice from Nandaka ",
  "mn146:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn146:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "mn146:2.1": "Then Mahāpajāpati Gotamī together with around five hundred nuns approached the Buddha, bowed, stood to one side, and said to him, ",
  "mn146:2.2": "“Sir, may the Buddha please advise ",
  "mn146:2.3": "and instruct the nuns. ",
  "mn146:2.4": "Please give the nuns a Dhamma talk.” ",
  "mn146:3.1": "Now at that time the senior monks were taking turns to advise the nuns. ",
  "mn146:3.2": "But Venerable Nandaka didn’t want to take his turn. ",
  "mn146:3.3": "Then the Buddha said to Venerable Ānanda, ",
  "mn146:3.4": "“Ānanda, whose turn is it to advise the nuns today?” ",
  "mn146:3.5": "“It’s Nandaka’s turn, sir, ",
  "mn146:3.6": "but he doesn’t want to do it.” ",
  "mn146:4.1": "Then the Buddha said to Nandaka, ",
  "mn146:4.2": "“Nandaka, please advise ",
  "mn146:4.3": "and instruct the nuns. ",
  "mn146:4.4": "Please, brahmin, give the nuns a Dhamma talk.” ",
  "mn146:4.5": "“Yes, sir,” replied Nandaka. Then, in the morning, he robed up and, taking his bowl and robe, entered Sāvatthī for alms. ",
  "mn146:4.6": "He wandered for alms in Sāvatthī. After the meal, on his return from almsround, he went to the Royal Monastery with a companion. ",
  "mn146:4.7": "Those nuns saw him coming off in the distance, ",
  "mn146: